  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5102.54 Millen Lake. Motorboats and outboard motors shall not be operated at a speed exceeding 10 miles per hour on Millen Lake in the town of Washington, provided, however, that this restriction shall not apply between the hours of 10:00 a.m. and 12:00 noon daily and between the hours of 2:30 p.m. and 5:30 p.m. daily.\n\nSource. #2351, eff 4-25-83; ss by #3010, eff 5-2-85; amd by #4347, eff 12-22-87; ss by #4562, eff 1-3-89; ss by #5936, INTERIM, eff 1-3-95, EXPIRES: 5-3-95; ss by #6005, eff 3-24-95; amd by #6768, EMERGENCY, eff 6-17-98, EXPIRES: 10-15-98; amd by #6773, EMERGENCY, eff 6-22-98, EXPIRED: 10-20-98; amd by #7534, eff 7-25-01; paragraphs (a)-(c) EXPIRED: 3-24-03\n\nNew: #7904, INTERIM, eff 6-24-03, EXPIRED: 12-21-03\n\nNew. #8107, EMERGENCY, eff 6-22-04, EXPIRES: 12-19-04, except for paragraph (d); ss and moved by #8172, eff 9-21-04 (from Saf-C 402.41) ; ss by #10169, EXEMPT, eff 8-8-12 (formerly Saf-C 402.49) (See Revision Note #2 at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5100)",
